'''Mount Tantiss''' was a [[mountain]] on the [[planet]] [[Wayland]] that hosted [[Tantiss Base]]. During the early days of the [[Imperial Era]], the [[Galactic Empire]] relocated its [[Imperial cloning program|cloning program]] from the extragalactic planet [[Kamino]] to the Wayland facility,<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> establishing it as the headquarters for the secret [[Advanced Science Division]].<ref name="Tipping Point" /> Medical personnel, including the kidnapped [[Nala Se]], were brought to Mount Tantiss for the cloning effort.<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> The mountain included several facilities for the cloning program including holding cells for Se<ref name="Metamorphosis">{{TBB|Metamorphosis (episode)}}</ref> and rogue [[Cloning|clones]],<ref name="Tipping Point">{{TBB|Tipping Point}}</ref> and an underground containment zone for cloned [[Zillo Beast]]s. Mount Tantiss and its facilities were heavily guarded by [[clone commando]]s, [[Imperial royal guard]]s, and [[TK stormtrooper]]s.<ref name="Metamorphosis" />

{{Nature-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Mount Tantiss first appeared in ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the [[August 13]], [[2021]] season one finale of the animated TV show ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'' named "[[Kamino Lost]],"<ref name="Kamino Lost" /> and was first identified as Mount Tantiss in the corresponding episode guide on [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="KL EG" /> In [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]], [[Mount Tantiss/Legends|Mount Tantiss]] was created by the author [[Timothy Zahn]] and first appeared in the [[1991]] novel ''[[Heir to the Empire]]''.<ref name="Heir to the Empire, 20th anniversary edition">''[[Heir to the Empire: The 20th Anniversary Edition]]''</ref> In the Legends continuity, Mount Tantiss was home to [[Emperor/Legends|Emperor]] [[Palpatine/Legends|Palpatine's]] secret storehouses, including thousands of [[Spaarti cloning cylinder]]s, making the installation related to Imperial cloning technology in both continuities.<ref name="The Last Command">''[[The Last Command]]''</ref>

